 born about B.C. 1035 (1 Chr. 22:5; 29:1).","verses":273,"father":"David","mother":"Bathsheba","v":[16]},{"id":"zephaniah_3039","name":"Zephaniah","also":"","summary":"The son of Maaseiah, the “second priest” in the reign of Zedekiah, often mentioned in Jeremiah as having been sent from the king to inquire (Jer. 21:1) regarding the coming woes which he had denounced, and to entreat the prophet’s intercession that the judgment threatened might be averted (Jer. 29:25, 26, 29; 37:3; 52:24).","verses":6,"father":"Maaseiah","mother":"","v":[18]},{"id":"seraiah_2494","name":"Seraiah","also":"","summary":"A ruler of the temple (Neh. 11:11).","verses":5,"father":"Azariah","mother":"","v":[18]},{"id":"gedaliah_1287","name":"Gedaliah","also":"","summary":"The son of Ahikam, and grandson of Shaphan, secretary of king Josiah (Jer. 26:24). After the destruction of Jerusalem (see ZEDEKIAH), Nebuchadnezzar left him to govern the country as tributary to him (2 Kings 25:22; Jer. 40:5; 52:16).","verses":26,"father":"Ahikam","mother":"","v":[22,23,24,25]},{"id":"shaphan_2550","name":"Shaphan","also":"","summary":"A coney, a scribe or secretary of king Josiah (2 Kings 22:3-7). He consulted Huldah concerning the newly-discovered copy of the law which was delivered to him by Hilkiah the priest (8-14).","verses":23,"father":"Azaliah","mother":"","v":[22]},{"id":"ahikam_141","name":"Ahikam","also":"","summary":"Brother of support = helper, one of the five whom Josiah sent to consult the prophetess Huldah in connection with the discovery of the book of the law (2 Kings 22:12-14; 2 Chr. 34:20).","verses":20,"father":"Shaphan","mother":"","v":[22]},{"id":"ishmael_631","name":"Ishmael","also":"","summary":"The son of Nethaniah, “of the seed royal” (Jer. 40:8, 15). He plotted against Gedaliah, and treacherously put him and others to death.","verses":21,"father":"Nethaniah","mother":"","v":[23,25]},{"id":"nethaniah_2198","name":"Nethaniah","also":"","summary":"2 Kings 25:23, 25.","verses":16,"father":"Elishama","mother":"","v":[23,25]},{"id":"johanan_1666","name":"Johanan","also":"","summary":"Son of Careah, one of the Jewish chiefs who rallied round Gedaliah, whom Nebuchadnezzar had made governor in Jerusalem (2 Kings 25:23; Jer. 40:8).","verses":15,"father":"Kareah","mother":"","v":[23]},{"id":"kareah_919","name":"Kareah","also":"Careah","summary":"Bald, the father of Johanan and Jonathan, who for a time were loyal to Gedaliah, the Babylonian governor of Jerusalem (Jer. 40:8, 13, 15, 16).","verses":14,"father":"","mother":"","v":[23]},{"id":"jezaniah_667","name":"Jezaniah","also":"Azariah, Jaazaniah","summary":"A Maachathite (2 Kings 25:23; Jer. 40:8; 42:1).","verses":4,"father":"Hoshaiah","mother":"","v":[23]},{"id":"seraiah_2495","name":"Seraiah","also":"","summary":"Captive by Nebuchadnezzar to Babylon.","verses":2,"father":"Tanhumeth","mother":"","v":[23]},{"id":"tanhumeth_2824","name":"Tanhumeth","also":"","summary":"Consolation, a Netophathite; one of the captains who supported Gedaliah (2 Kings 25:23; Jer. 40:8).","verses":2,"father":"","mother":"","v":[23]},{"id":"elishama_1157","name":"Elishama","also":"","summary":"","verses":2,"father":"","mother":"","v":[25]},{"id":"jehoiachin_791","name":"Jehoiachin","also":"Jeconiah, Coniah, Jechonias","summary":"Succeeded his father Jehoiakin (B.C. 599) when only eight years of age, and reigned for one hundred days (2 Chr. 36:9). He is also called Jeconiah (Jer. 24:1; 27:20, etc.), and Coniah (22:24; 37:1).","verses":21,"father":"Jehoiakim","mother":"Nehushta","v":[27]},{"id":"evil-merodach_1233","name":"Evil-merodach","also":"","summary":"Merodach’s man, the son and successor of Nebuchadnezzar, king of Babylon (2 Kings 25:27; Jer. 52:31, 34). He seems to have reigned but two years (B.C. 562-560).","verses":2,"father":"","mother":"","v":[27]}],"places":[{"id":"babylon_151","name":"Babylon","kind":"City","lat":32.53617,"lon":44.42082,"summary":"The Greek form of BABEL; Semitic form Babilu, meaning “The Gate of God.” In the Assyrian tablets it means “The city of the dispersion of the tribes.”","verses":255,"v":[1,6,7,8,11,13,20,21,22,23,24,27,28]},{"id":"jerusalem_636","name":"Jerusalem","kind":"City","lat":31.77667,"lon":35.23417,"summary":"Called also Salem, Ariel, Jebus, the “city of God,” the “holy city;” by the modern Arabs el-Khuds, meaning “the holy;” once “the city of Judah” (2 Chr. 25:28).","verses":754,"v":[1,8,9,10]},{"id":"arabah_79","name":"Arabah","kind":"","lat":32.02968,"lon":35.52099,"summary":"Plain, in the Revised Version of 2 Kings 14:25; Josh. 3:16; 8:14; 2 Sam. 2:29; 4:7 (in all these passages the A.V. has “plain”); Amos 6:14 (A.V. “wilderness”).","verses":15,"v":[4]},{"id":"jericho_634","name":"Jericho","kind":"City","lat":31.87005,"lon":35.44388,"summary":"Place of fragrance, a fenced city in the midst of a vast grove of palm trees, in the plain of Jordan, over against the place where that river was crossed by the Israelites (Josh. 3:16).","verses":58,"v":[5]},{"id":"riblah_1001","name":"Riblah","kind":"City","lat":34.4317,"lon":36.54526,"summary":"Fruitful, an ancient town on the northern frontier of Palestine, 35 miles north-east of Baalbec, and 10 or 12 south of Lake Homs, on the eastern bank of the Orontes, in a wide and fertile plain.","verses":11,"v":[6,20,21]},{"id":"hamath_516","name":"Hamath","kind":"City","lat":35.1359,"lon":36.7495,"summary":"Fortress, the capital of one of the kingdoms of Upper Syria of the same name, on the Orontes, in the valley of Lebanon, at the northern boundary of Palestine (Num. 13:21; 34:8), at the foot of Hermon (Josh. 13:5) towards Damascus (Zech. 9:2; Jer. 49:23).","verses":23,"v":[21]},{"id":"mizpah_811","name":"Mizpah","kind":"City","lat":31.83274,"lon":35.18016,"summary":"A city of Benjamin, “the watch-tower”, where the people were accustomed to meet in great national emergencies (Josh. 18:26; Judg. 20:1, 3; 21:1, 5; 1 Sam. 7:5-16).","verses":30,"v":[23,25]},{"id":"egypt_362","name":"Egypt","kind":"Region (Country)","lat":26.4902,"lon":29.8808,"summary":"The land of the Nile and the pyramids, the oldest kingdom of which we have any record, holds a place of great significance in Scripture.","verses":564,"v":[26]}],"events":[{"id":"reign_of_zedekiah_242","title":"Reign of Zedekiah","year":-597,"summary":"Passage: 2 Kings 24:18–25:7. People: Zedekiah. Place: Jerusalem. Lasted about 11 years.","v":[1,2,3,4,5,6,7]}],"traditions":[],"sources":["JFB","MHCC","Wesley"],"tags":{"bsb":[[1961,8671,8671,8671,8141,4427,4427,4427,6218,6218,6218,6224,6224,6224,6224,2320,5019,4428,894,894,935,5921,3389,3605,3605,3605,2428,2583,2583,5921,5921,5921,1129,1129,1785,1785,1785,5439,5439,5439],[5892,5892,5892,935,935,4692,4692,5704,4428,6667,6249,8141],[8672,8672,8672,8672,2320,2320,2320,2320,7458,7458,5892,5892,5892,2388,2388,2388,5971,5971,5971,776,776,776,1961,3808,3899],[5892,5892,5892,1234,1234,3778,3778,3778,3778,5439,5439,5892,5892,3605,582,582,4421,4421,3915,3915,3915,1870,1870,8179,8179,8179,996,2346,2346,2346,5921,4428,4428,1588,1980,1980,1870,6160,6160],[2428,2428,2428,3778,3778,3778,7291,4428,4428,5381,5381,853,6160,6160,6160,3405,3405,3605,3605,3605,2428,6327,5921],[8610,8610,8610,4428,4428,5927,5927,5927,5927,413,4428,4428,894,894,7247,7247,1696,1696,1696,4941,854,854],[853,7819,7819,1121,1121,6667,6667,5869,5869,5869,853,5786,5786,5786,6667,5869,631,631,5178,5178,5178,935,935,935,894,894],[7651,7651,7651,2549,2549,2549,2549,2320,8672,8672,8672,8141,5019,5019,4428,894,894,5018,7227,2876,2876,2876,5650,5650,4428,4428,4428,894,894,935,3389],[8313,8313,8313,1004,1004,3068,3068,3068,4428,4428,1004,3605,3605,1004,1004,3389,3389,1419,1004],[3605,3605,3605,2428,3778,3778,3778,834,7227,7227,2876,2876,2876,5422,5422,2346,2346,5439,3389],[5018,5018,7227,2876,2876,2876,1540,1540,1540,5971,5971,7604,7604,5892,5892,5892,853,853,5307,5307,834,5307,5307,5921,4428,4428,894,894,3499,3499,3499,1995,1995,1995],[7227,7227,7227,2876,2876,2876,7604,7604,1803,1803,1803,1803,776,776,776,3755,3755,